  "prose": [
    {
      "title": "Example",
      "text": "Carousels don’t automatically normalize slide dimensions. As such, you\nmay need to use additional utilities or custom styles to appropriately\nsize content. While carousels support previous/next controls and\nindicators, they’re not explicitly required. Add and customize as you\nsee fit.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Controlled",
      "text": "You can also _control_ the Carousel state, via the\n`activeIndex` prop and `onSelect` handler.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Crossfade",
      "text": "Add the `fade` prop to your carousel to animate slides with a fade transition instead of a slide.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "No transition animation",
      "text": "Set the `slide` prop to false to disable the transition animation between slides.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Individual Item Intervals",
      "text": "You can specify individual intervals for each carousel item via the `interval`\nprop.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Dark variant",
      "text": "Add `variant=\"dark\"` to the `Carousel` for darker controls, indicators, and captions.\n\n:::caution Heads up!\n\nDark variants for components were deprecated in Bootstrap v5.3.0 with the introduction\nof color modes. Instead of adding `variant=\"dark\"`, set `data-bs-theme=\"dark\"` on the root\nelement, a parent wrapper, or the component itself.\n\n:::",
      "format": "md"
    }
  ],
